; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The research description spans roughly 27°S–40°S; the coastal path is longer than its north–south separation. Retroflection, leakage, and the eastward Agulhas Return Current are distinct from this boundary-current core. The derived floor is unranked. A 2021 review also describes a roughly 1,000 km coastal segment. That narrower usage conflicts with the broader 27°S–40°S derived floor, so the two numbers are displayed as source-specific scopes and neither is ranked as a common whole-current length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marine_info_guide.pdf","source_decision":{"current_id":"agulhas","name":"Agulhas Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"derived_lower_bound","existing_scope":"The research description spans roughly 27°S–40°S; the coastal path is longer than its north–south separation. Retroflection, leakage, and the eastward Agulhas Return Current are distinct from this boundary-current core. The derived floor is unranked. A 2021 review also describes a roughly 1,000 km coastal segment. That narrower usage conflicts with the broader 27°S–40°S derived floor, so the two numbers are displayed as source-specific scopes and neither is ranked as a common whole-current length.","name_source_url":"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marine_info_guide.pdf","candidate_ids":["agulhas-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"western boundary current","route_strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","route_strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The research description spans roughly 27°S–40°S; the coastal path is longer than its north–south separation. Retroflection, leakage, and the eastward Agulhas Return Current are distinct from this boundary-current core. The derived floor is unranked. A 2021 review also describes a roughly 1,000 km coastal segment. That narrower usage conflicts with the broader 27°S–40°S derived floor, so the two numbers are displayed as source-specific scopes and neither is ranked as a common whole-current length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:agulhas-return","entity_id":"current:agulhas-return","label":"Agulhas Return Current","current_id":"agulhas-return","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":2,"route_ids":["agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate","agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The hydrographic survey distinguishes the Agulhas Return Current from the Agulhas Current and traces its weakening eastward flow toward the Crozet Basin. This derived distance floor is not a measured streamline, whole-current length, or the length of the westward Agulhas Current.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classifica