tic front and Isoguchi jets","locator":"Introduction, first Results subsection, Figure 1 caption; Methods Data.","access":"Relevant repository PDF text read; gradient front and search window are not velocity boundaries."}],"related_proposed_current_ids":["alaskan-stream","aleutian-north-slope"],"related_proposed_currents":[{"id":"alaskan-stream","name":"Alaskan Stream"},{"id":"aleutian-north-slope","name":"Aleutian North Slope Current"}]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-naming-scope-audit.v1","date":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_scope_audit_not_scientific_approval","current_id":"aleutian","name":"Aleutian Current","alias":"Subarctic Current","primary_definition":{"url":"https://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/aleutian-current/","access":"full_page_read","locator":"Definition paragraphs","interpretation":"Eastward southern limb of the subpolar gyre; Oyashio outflow feeds it and eastern flow divides toward Alaska and California. No source-defined endpoint coordinates."},"distinct_proposed_current":"alaskan-stream","proposal_source":"research/ocean-current-inventory-expansion-candidates.json","length_decision":"unknown_whole_current_endpoints_regional_editorial_reach_available","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"stream_study_context":{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2016JC012302","citation":"Logan and Johnson (2017), doi:10.1002/2016JC012302","access":"full_page_read","locator":"Introduction; sections 2 and 3; figure 1 caption","limits":"Study coverage and offshore section windows do not define named-flow endpoints or full widths. Pressure-reference velocity estimates remain separate from measured full-depth velocity."},"remaining_gates":["Diagnose Aleutian source-interface and eastern split with defensible time/layer support.","Preserve North Pacific Current exchange and frontage without treating mixing as a unique centerline.","Review Alaskan Stream identity separately; do not reuse any Aleutian geometry or length.","Separate cold Subarctic flow from warm Isoguchi jets; SST search bounds are not current gates or width edges."],"distinct_proposed_currents":["alaskan-stream","aleutian-north-slope"],"north_slope_review":{"url":"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/stab1878/stab1878.shtml","access":"Relevant HTML circulation subsections and captions read; no figure digitization or underlying field acquisition.","locator":"Mean Upper Ocean Circulation, Alaskan Stream / Aleutian North Slope Current / Bering Slope Current.","proposed_identity":"aleutian-north-slope","scope":"Bering-side pass-fed regional flow; not an alias of Aleutian/Subarctic Current.","regional_width_context_km":20,"numeric_context_role":"author_described_ANSC_regional_width_not_Aleutian_width","whole_current_dimension_eligible":false,"source_conflict":"Bering Slope Current paragraph prints 167 N; nearby ANSC context uses 167 W. Retained as source wording, not an endpoint coordinate."},"western_front_review":{"url":"https://eprints.lib.hokudai.ac.jp/repo/huscap/all/70589/naturecommunications9_1190.pdf","citation":"Mitsudera et al. (2018), doi:10.1038/s41467-018-03526-z.","access":"Repository PDF introduction, first Results subsection, Figure 1 caption and Methods Data subsection read; source fields and figures not digitized.","locator":"Printed pp. 2–3 and 9 (PDF indices 2–3 and 9).","interpretation":"Warm northeastward Isoguchi J1/J2 meet cold Subarctic flow. Maximum SST-gradient front is not a unique velocity axis or paired current-width boundary.","front_search_domain_lon_lat":[145,170,35,47],"domain_role":"SST_front_search_window_not_current_extent","jcope2_years":[1993,2013],"jcope2_grid_degrees":0.08333333333333333,"observed_route_coordinates":null,"paired_width_edges":null},"access_failures":[{"url":"https://floats.pmel.noaa.gov/sites/default/files/atoms/files/Alaskan_Stream_v2.pdf","result":"HTTP 5