lish a whole-current path or length and does not resolve flow farther south.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":["antilles-northern-bahamas-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"regional current with disputed northern surface expression","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"NOAA's six sections near 28°35′N found variable northward and southward bands rather than the broad, persistent northward surface current shown on older charts. This section cannot establish a whole-current path or length and does not resolve flow farther south.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"antilles","label":"Modern regional mean versus historical surface assessment","audit_file":"research/antilles-current-naming-seasonal-scope-audit.json","summary":"Modern observations support mean northward flow at 26.5 N, distinct from the older northern surface-flow assessment. Neither study defines whole-current endpoint coordinates. Table 3 gives a 49.4 km coast-to-site-B transport integration span, not current width; instrument positions are not along-current endpoints. Weak August-September transport maximum does not establish seasonal route geometry.","source_url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/20909/noaa_20909_DS1.pdf","source_locator":"Introduction, section 3.1, Table 1, Table 3 (PDF page 15), seasonal discussion/Fig. 11 and Conclusions","observed_period":{"start":"2005-05-08","end":"2015-11-23"}},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-naming-scope-audit.v1","date":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_scope_audit_not_scientific_approval","current_id":"antilles","name":"Antilles Current","sources":[{"url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/20909/noaa_20909_DS1.pdf","citation":"Meinen et al. (2019), Structure and Variability of the Antilles Current at 26.5 N, doi:10.1029/2018JC014836","access":"full_repository_pdf_read","locator":"Introduction pp. 1-2; Table 1 p. 3; section 3.1; Table 3 p. 15; seasonal discussion and Fig. 11 pp. 17-18; Conclusions. PDF page numbers.","supports":"Regional mean northward flow at 26.5 N with subsurface peak and intermittent reversal; nominal instrument locations and a declared transport integration domain. Weak transport seasonality does not define route or width extrema.","observed_period":{"start":"2005-05-08","end":"2015-11-23"}},{"url":"https://spo.nmfs.noaa.gov/sites/default/files/pdf-content/1975/733/ingham.pdf","citation":"Ingham (1975), Velocity and transport of the Antilles Current northeast of the Bahama Islands","access":"previously_read_in_released_source_review","locator":"Six sections near 28 degrees 35 minutes N","supports":"Older geographically distinct surface-flow assessment; cannot establish absence at every depth, place or time."},{"url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","citation":"NOAA Tides and Currents Glossary, Antilles Current entry","access":"full_page_read","locator":"Antilles Current entry","supports":"General northwestward named flow along the northeastern Bahamas; no numerical endpoints."}],"identity_decision":"retain_named_current_with_separate_historical_surface_and_modern_regional_mean_support","scope_summary":"Modern observations support mean northward flow at 26.5 N, distinct from the older northern surface-flow assessment. Neither study defines whole-current endpoint coordinates.","length_decision":"whole_current_route_unknown_no_source_defined_endpoints","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"rejected_width_inference":{"reported_span_km":49.4,"source_locator":"Table 3, coastline to site B transport-integration domain","measurement_role":"transport_integration_span_not_diagnosed_current_width","admitted_as_width":false},"source_access_note":"Publisher full page returned 403; NOAA repository PDF read. No source curve digitized. Final AB0505 LADCP ASCII profiles and provider assessment were acquired separately in October 2026 and pinned with per-file checksums; this does not supply a longitudinal axis.","remaining_gates":["Diagnose named-flow endpoints and representative velocity axis with declared layer and dates.","Specify a physical width boundary before deriving section widths; integration spans are a separate quantity.","Reconcile method-dependent velocity estimates before seasonal geometry and annual extrema.","Review updated scientific scope and rights before modifying the frozen release."],"source_locator_correction":{"rechecked_date":"2026-10-03","previous_locator":"Table 5","correct_locator":"Table 3, PDF page 15 / journal page 3714","source_url":"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/20909/noaa_20909_DS1.pdf","verification":"Table heading and coastline-to-site-B row checked in NOAA repository and AOML copies; no Table 5 present in either text."},"local_section_support":{"section_latitude_degrees_north":26.5,"coordinate_role":"nominal_instrument_locations_not_current_edges_or_along_stream_endpoints","crs":"OGC:CRS84","source_locator":"Table 1, PDF page 3 / journal page 3702","sites":[{"id":"A","coordinates_lon_lat":[-76.83,26.52]},{"id":"A2","coordinates_lon_lat":[-76.75,26.5]},{"id":"B","coordinates_lon_lat":[-76.47,26.49]},{"id":"C","coordinates_lon_lat":[-76.09,26.5]}],"mean_structure_context":{"peak_pressure_dbar_approximate":400,"near_zero_pressure_dbar_approximate":900,"source_locator":"Section 3.1 and Figure 2 caption; mean of 16 LADCP sections","whole_current_layer_bounds_inferred":false},"transport_integration_domain":{"reported_span_km":49.4,"horizontal_convention":"coastline to site B","vertical_convention":"surface to 1000 dbar or bottom where shallower","source_locator":"Table 3, PDF page 15 / journal page 3714","is_current_width":false,"is_along_current_length":false,"site_B_is_instantaneous_current_edge":false},"seasonal_context":{"maximum_northward_transport_months":[8,9],"measurement":"regional transport climatology, not geometry","source_locator":"Seasonal discussion and Fig. 11, PDF pages 17-18","qualifier":"Weak seasonal component; large error bars; previous shorter-record cycle differs. No annual dimension extrema or dated axes inferred.","eligible_for_geometry_animation":false}},"data_acquisition_review_date":"2026-10-04","acquired_profile_context":{"inventory_file":"research/antilles-ab0505-ladcp-profile-inventory.json","inventory_sha256":"491fbe8feb7393600888455c26390d67fe0a734ab2e248d9a0474161a0437227","diagnostic_file":"research/antilles-ab0505-400m-section-diagnostic.json","provider":"NOAA/AOML/PhOD WBTS","profile_count":57,"depth_samples":22619,"provider_usable_count":40,"provider_caution_count":17,"abaco_first_casts":23,"abaco_repeat_casts":27,"other_section_casts_excluded":7,"status":"acquired_profiles_and_derived_one_sided_diagnostic_not_full_width_admission","summary":"At fixed 400 m instrument depth, first May 2005 section is blocked by caution casts. Repeat has about 37 km sampled-peak-to-offshore-half-peak span, not full width. Source quality comments, unremoved tides, error velocities, missing-depth samples and cast times are retained. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved."}},"source_sha256":"2b6b59af048ac032cfd87f3ebf02fd4f1b972f8aafef3c5c7f9574183894b9cb"}]},{"id":"route-decision:atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent","current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"A PIRATA ADCP observed the current at 0°N, 23°W in 2002; the station is not a whole-current length. Lomonosov is an established alternate name; Marine Regions spells it Lomonoscov.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=30077","source_decision":{"current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","name":"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"A PIRATA ADCP observed the current at 0°N, 23°W in 2002; the station is not a whole-current length. Lomonosov is an established alternate name; Marine Regions spells it Lomonoscov.","name_source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=30077","candidate_ids":["atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"eastward subsurface jet","route_strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","route_strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"A PIRATA ADCP observed the current at 0°N, 23°W in 2002; the station is not a whole-current length. Lomonosov is an established alternate name; Marine Regions spells it Lomonoscov.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"Atlantic subsurface reach and island bifurcation scope","audit_file":"research/atlantic-euc-layer-island-scope-audit.json","summary":"Declared 35 Wâ€“5 E subsurface reach excludes upstream retroflections and the Sao Tome bifurcation. Surface currents, deeper jets and modeled island-generated eddies remain distinct; whole-current dimensions and seasonal geometry unresolved.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2022-11/010086132.pdf","source_locator":"Introduction pp. 1â€“2 and observation/model sections 2â€“3.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-08","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_access":[{"url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2022-11/010086132.pdf","status":"full_primary_institutional_pdf_read","doi":"10.1029/2021JC017999","supports":"Eastward equatorial subsurface jet encounters Sao Tome and bifurcates; model eddies and return flows remain distinct from named source identities."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2006JC003931","status":"full_primary_publisher_page_read","doi":"10.1029/2006JC003931","supports":"35 W equatorial observational section and approximately 100 m core; depth/time/model distinctions."},{"url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/cahiers/ocea_tro/15471.pdf","status":"institutional_original_pdf_visually_reviewed","supports":"Campaign core speed/depth and unresolved Table I/II date conflicts; Figure 2 dated velocity sections, not extracted horizontal widths."}],"declared_gates":{"west":[-35,0],"east":[5,0],"role":"editorial_truncation_not_whole_current_endpoints"},"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"source_scope":"Subsurface equatorial/thermocline jet. At 35 W the reported mean observed core is about 100 m; eastern cores and isopycnal layers differ. No single depth is imposed on the route; surface SEC/NECC and deeper equatorial currents remain separate.","excluded_inferences":["Do not treat source transport changes or vertical thickness as horizontal width.","Do not transfer surface NASA swirls to thermocline current identification.","Do not identify modeled island-generated anticyclones as named registry eddies.","Do not compare this truncated reach directly with whole Pacific EUC length."],"remaining_gates":["Review 35 W and pre-island truncation; source retroflections and eastern branches are not represented.","Obtain compatible depth/time-resolved velocity axis before physical length or seasonal dimensions.","Resolve island interaction and return-flow topology without treating generated eddies as named identities.","No occupied footprint, route-buffer width or whole-basin system length inferred.","Resolve campaign 7910/7912 Table I/II date conflicts before dated frames.","Extract reproducible paired velocity edges from original sections before assigning local horizontal width."],"section_properties":{"schema":"osw.atlantic-euc-section-properties.v1","current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/cahiers/ocea_tro/15471.pdf","source_document_file":"research/source-data/voituriez-atlantic-euc-1983/journal-article.pdf","source_document_sha256":"a1c4b1dfc46247cb9c7da90ea03aa1a240bc987bd26b21c9cdf49f027d457e0b","source_document_bytes":1887693,"acquisition_file":"research/source-data/voituriez-atlantic-euc-1983/acquisition.json","acquisition_sha256":"1734746902c37f4fe31bc0dbf2a39b6f173a96e0759aa7604257683cca32736b","protocol_file":"plans/atlantic-euc-section-properties-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"4d8ff5480aba2d14be3d3a082e805f9b90843c2db5fb6ef52bc46f1d596a068e","source_locator":"Printed pp165,167–168: Table I, Figure 2, Table II; methods pp164–165.","section_longitude_deg_e":-4,"station_latitude_deg":null,"velocity_reference_depth_m":500,"reference_assumption":"500 m assumed motionless; drifting-ship Aanderaa profiler.","transport_context":{"eastward_speed_threshold_cm_s":20,"depth_bounds_m":[0,200],"is_horizontal_width_definition":false},"uncertainty_cm_s":null,"core_depth_uncertainty_m":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"width_inference_eligible":false,"occupied_geometry_eligible":false,"date_conflict_count":2,"display_caption":"Eight campaign core-property records at 4°W, in printed table order. Speed maxima and their depths are distinct from horizontal width. Hollow points have unresolved dates; no interpolated seasonal cycle.","records":[{"id":"atlantic-euc-cap-7701","campaign":"7701","station_label":"26","table_ii_date_text":"Jan 77","table_i_campaign_period":"January 1977","date_conflict":false,"resolved_observation_date":null,"maximum_eastward_speed_cm_s":98,"maximum_speed_depth_m":65},{"id":"atlantic-euc-cap-7706","campaign":"7706","station_label":"7","table_ii_date_text":"Jul 7