ecadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2006GL026965","candidate_ids":["deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"deep western boundary current","route_strategy_id":"system_route_graph","route_strategy_label":"Define system and branch graph","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The study identifies southward deep western boundary flow at 47°, 36°, and 24.5°N in decadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:east-adriatic","entity_id":"current:east-adriatic","label":"East Adriatic Current","current_id":"east-adriatic","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271","source_decision":{"current_id":"east-adriatic","name":"East Adriatic Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271","candidate_ids":["east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"northwestward coastal boundary current","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"east-adriatic","label":"East Adriatic naming and extent convention","audit_file":"research/east-adriatic-naming-extent-scope-audit.json","summary":"Eastern-coast northwestward circulation convention is distinct from the western return and basin gyres. Otranto-to-Istria context is not a diagnosed whole-current axis; Dalmatian-name overlap remains unresolved, and 800 km basin length is not current length.","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","source_locator":"Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern-coast EAC, separate southeastward western-coast WAC, three sub-basin recirculations, wind modulation.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"east-adriatic","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","source_access":"publisher_full_text_relevant_background_and_figure_caption_read","source_citation":"Sciascia et al. (2018), Linking sardine recruitment in coastal areas to ocean currents using surface drifters and HF radar: a case study in the Gulf of Manfredonia, Adriatic Sea. Ocean Science 14, 1461-1482, doi:10.5194/os-14-1461-2018.","source_locator":"Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern-coast EAC, separate southeastward western-coast WAC, three sub-basin recirculations, wind modulation.","naming_decision":{"ledger_label":"East Adriatic Current","source_label":"Eastern Adriatic Current","assignment":"Editorial alignment of the same eastern-coast northwestward circulation convention; no new canonical alias admitted.","dalmatian_name_synonymy":"unresolved_not_merged"},"geographic_conventions":[{"url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/","locator":"Section 2.1 and Figure 1","scope":"Northwestward eastern Balkan coast; distinct western return current and recirculation gyres. The stated 800 by 200 km dimensions describe the Adriatic basin, not the EAC length or width.","access":"publisher_relevant_sections_read","source_license":"Publisher states Creative Commons Attribution 4.0; no source figure or drifter data copied."},{"url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.00679/full","locator":"Study area, mean circulation paragraph citing Poulain (2001)","scope":"Background convention extends EAC northward from Otranto toward the Istrian Peninsula. This is regional circulation context, not a diagnosed continuous axis or formal current termination.","access":"publisher_relevant_study_area_text_read","source_license":"Not independently reviewed in this audit; attributed textual facts only."}],"original_measurement_source":{"url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271","citation":"Orlic et al. (2006), Wintertime buoyancy forcing, changing seawater properties, and two different circulation systems produced in the Adriatic.","access":"Publisher full text inaccessible in this turn; author-hosted search excerpt found but full page access returned HTTP 429. No new values extracted.","existing_ledger_scope":"2002-2003 local eastern-coast measurements; no full path length admitted."},"layer":"General surface circulation context in the two accessed papers. Intermediate-water inflow is not assigned the same route or a uniform full-depth layer.","observed_period":null,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","proposed_gate_regions":["Eastern Otranto inflow neighborhood","Offshore western/southern Istrian neighborhood"],"exclusions":["Western Adriatic return flow","Northern, central and southern recirculation loops","Individually unverified island-channel branches","Dalmatian-name extent transfer"],"remaining_gates":["Choose explicit offshore gate coordinates and alternative coastal paths with the same convention.","Screen all declared paths against the coarse land geometry, then review islands and narrow passages using finer bathymetry.","Retain the regional convention and unresolved Dalmatian naming in every length record; do not borrow 800 km basin length.","Retrieve original measurement and drifter papers before claiming a diagnosed axis, seasonal footprint, or numeric current width."],"candidate_file":"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-input.json","route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":800,"reported_scenario_range_km":[700,800],"scenario_count":81,"source_basin_dimension_not_used":true,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false}},"source_sha256":"435ae6d4d1dae6f6a6c4be949d42118efc1158d349584271538ae32ec550c7d1"}]},{"id":"route-decision:east-australian","entity_id":"current:east-australian","label":"East Australian Current","current_id":"east-australian","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["east-australian-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marine_info_guide.pdf","source_decision":{"current_id":"east-australian","name":"East Australian Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"derived_lower_bound","existing_scope":"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.","name_source_url":"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marine_info_guide.pdf","candidate_ids":["east-australian-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"western boundary current","route_strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","route_strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:east-greenland-coastal","entity_id":"current:east-greenland-coastal","label":"East Greenland Coastal Current","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","strategy_id":"preserve_survey_reach","strategy_label":"Preserve surveyed-reach scope","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_decision":{"current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","name":"East Greenland Coastal Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"sampled_reach_only","existing_scope":"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.","name_source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","candidate_ids":["east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"low-salinity inner-shelf coastal jet","route_strategy_id":"preserve_survey_reach","route_strategy_label":"Preserve surveyed-reach scope","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Reconstruct only the source survey reach first; obtain independent start/end evidence before proposing a broader current route.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","label":"Coastal studied reach, northern uncertainty and local threshold width","audit_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-scope-audit.json","summary":"The 66 N to Cape Farewell editorial reach is separate from the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey. Weak northern identification and merging near 63 N limit continuity claims. The 30 km Cape Farewell width uses a 15% inner-jet velocity threshold and cannot buffer this whole route or supply annual margins.","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"east-greenland-coastal","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf","source_access":"Accepted manuscript relevant sections 3, 8 and 9 read; source figure screenshot unavailable; no axis digitized. Width sections 2 and 3.1 inspected in previous extraction.","source_citation":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), The East Greenland Coastal Current: Structure, variability, and forcing, Progress in Oceanography, accepted manuscript.","source_locator":"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.","scope":"Declared southeast Greenland coastal study-area reach from an OSW offshore gate near 66 N to a Cape Farewell offshore gate near 60 N. Excludes the weak northern 68 N identification, EGC shelfbreak path, Irminger Current, offshore diversions and West Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.","layer":"Surface-intensified low-salinity inner-shelf jet context from July-August 2004 hydrography and ADCP-referenced geostrophic velocity. No uniform fixed-depth axis diagnosed along this editorial path.","observed_period":null,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"candidate_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","input_file":"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-input.json","source_shelf_reach_km":1000,"source_shelf_reach_is_current_axis_length":false,"local_width_measurement_id":"east-greenland-coastal-2004-cape-farewell-threshold-section","local_width_km":30,"local_width_velocity_fraction":0.15,"local_width_is_route_buffer":false,"route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":800,"reported_scenario_range_km":[800,900],"scenario_count":81,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false},"remaining_gates":["Review finer coastline and shelf bathymetry before claiming an inner-shelf current axis.","Resolve northern identification and the 63 N merger before any whole-current extent.","Do not replace the source approximately 1000 km shelf survey description with this shorter editorial reach.","Retain the Cape Farewell 30 km threshold width as a local section; no width buffer or annual footprint inferred."]},"source_sha256":"60349cb57aac6f8602f87b8b88ba3341e39a29cdc603a20aa50d6b9cd92e4ce1"}]},{"id":"route-decision:east-greenland","entity_id":"current:east-greenland","label":"East Greenland Current","current_id":"east-greenland","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["east-greenland-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"east-greenland","name":"East Greenland Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"derived_lower_bound","existing_scope":"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":["east-greenland-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"polar boundary current","route_strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","route_strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:equatorial-countercurrent","entity_id":"current:equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Equatorial Countercurrent","current_id":"equatorial-countercurrent","strategy_id":"split_basin_family","strategy_label":"Split basin families","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate