nality differ from the Atlantic flow. No comparable whole-current length is admitted.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","label":"March-May modeled reach and threshold-core spatial width","audit_file":"research/indian-seuc-mam-layer-core-scope-audit.json","summary":"March-May BRAN climatology supports a subsurface reach with OSW connecting vertices. Reported threshold-core widths vary across longitudes, not across seasons; density-layer context is separate from the three-dimensional core extent. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved. Source latitude and mooring-end-month inconsistencies are retained in the audit.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163","source_locator":"Sections 2-4 and Figure 2-3 captions","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163","source_citation":"Chen, Han, Zu, Chu and Chen (2022), The Deep-Penetrating South Equatorial Undercurrent in the Tropical South Indian Ocean, Geophysical Research Letters 49, e2022GL098163, doi:10.1029/2022GL098163.","source_locator":"Sections 2-4, Figures 1-3 captions and Erratum.","source_access":"Full publisher HTML relevant text and captions inspected; no figure digitized, BRAN field acquired or Supporting Information inspected.","scope":"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.","layer":"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.","time_convention":"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.","observed_period":null,"route_candidate_file":"research/indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","model_context":{"product":"BRAN2020","horizontal_resolution_degrees":0.1,"monthly_climatology_years":[2001,2018],"season_months":[3,4,5],"reference_density_range_sigma0":[27.9,28.7],"mooring_depth_conversion_is_uniform_basin_layer":false},"core_width_context":{"measurement_id":"indian-seuc-bran-mam-core-spatial-summary","velocity_component":"eastward_zonal_u","strict_threshold_m_s":0.1,"statistic":"median_across_longitudes","reported_median_km":169,"reported_spatial_range_km":[26,294],"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"fixed_depth_width":false},"source_consistency_notes":["One Results paragraph prints 10 N; abstract, mooring location and reach discussion give southern latitude. Typo retained as source conflict, not silently corrected.","Methods gives mooring August 2019-May 2020; Figure 1 caption says June 2020. No exact observation endpoint assigned.","Main occurrence January-June and weakening July-August differ from the Discussion January-August wording; this candidate uses March-May only.","Erratum supplies missing Figure 2 units; corrected HTML consulted."],"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"remaining_gates":["Extract compatible BRAN density-layer core geometry and review ridge-scale continuity before interpreting the connecting line as an axis.","Resolve source latitude typo (10 N in one paragraph versus 8-10 S elsewhere); southern context is used explicitly.","Review endpoint definitions and extensions before whole-current length.","Recover repeated matched axes and core boundaries before annual length/width extrema or seasonal playback."]},"source_sha256":"ee9f1525d6a8c0613bcd27f12d70265f0cf953f7f9815c3e625a4cf7b53a7627"}]},{"id":"route-decision:indonesian-throughflow","entity_id":"current:indonesian-throughflow","label":"Indonesian Throughflow","current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","strategy_id":"system_route_graph","strategy_label":"Define system and branch graph","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Use the source-described network in research/indonesian-throughflow-network-input.json to select individual layer-compatible branches and independently justify gateway/axis conventions. Twelve nodes and fourteen conceptual connections are queryable, with separate exit observations. No sum of branch lengths, scalar whole-system length or physical width follows from connectivity.","scope":"NASA names the Pacific-to-Indian freshwater passage through narrow gaps of the Maritime Continent but gives no single current centerline or whole-system length. This is a multi-channel flow, so no length enters the ranking.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5425","source_decision":{"current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","name":"Indonesian Throughflow","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"NASA names the Pacific-to-Indian freshwater passage through narrow gaps of the Maritime Continent but gives no single current centerline or whole-system length. This is a multi-channel flow, so no length enters the ranking.","name_source_url":"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5425","candidate_ids":[],"reference_path_decision":"reference_path_not_constructed","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"interbasin passage system","route_strategy_id":"system_route_graph","route_strategy_label":"Define system and branch graph","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"NASA names the Pacific-to-Indian freshwater passage through narrow gaps of the Maritime Continent but gives no single current centerline or whole-system length. This is a multi-channel flow, so no length enters the ranking.","next_action":"Use the source-described network in research/indonesian-throughflow-network-input.json to select individual layer-compatible branches and independently justify gateway/axis conventions. Twelve nodes and fourteen conceptual connections are queryable, with separate exit observations. No sum of branch lengths, scalar whole-system length or physical width follows from connectivity.","strategy_next_action":"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","label":"Source-described passage network and exit observations","audit_file":"research/indonesian-throughflow-network-scope-audit.json","summary":"Twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen selected passage connections; three 2004–2006 exit transport means and eight published mooring sites. No whole-system length, geographic graph edges or transfer of integration widths to physical current width.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3–4, Tables 1–2 and section 2.2","observed_period":{"start_year":2004,"end_year":2006,"precision":"year"}},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","as_of":"2026-10-04","status":"source_supported_conceptual_network_not_scientific_taxonomy_admission","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_access":"Publisher Introduction paragraphs 3–8, Tables 1–2 and section 2.2 read; no figure, field or transport time-series digitized.","source_locator":"Introduction paragraphs 3–4; Tables 1–2; section 2.2.","network_file":"research/indonesian-throughflow-network-input.json","summary":"Selected western/eastern inflow and three main exit pathways represented as twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen connections. Three exit transport means retain 2004–2006 support, processing-choice intervals and eight published first-deployment mooring positions. No geographic network edges, full system length, current width, annual extrema or instantaneous one-way-flow claim.","observed_period":{"start_year":2004,"end_year":2006,"precision":"year"},"source_time_caution":"Abstract mentions January 2003; Table 1 explicitly reports 2004–2006 averages. Individual mooring deployment dates differ, including an August 2003 Ombai deployment. Preserve these distinctions.","integration_width_caution":"35/35/160 km are transport-integration widths, not current widths. Ombai geographic width is discussed as 37 km in paragraph 8, while transport calculations use 35 km. Neither provides a uniform current footprint.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"rank_eligible":false,"canonical_taxonomy_admitted":false,"remaining_gates":["Assess full passage/depth coverage and reversals; no complete network asserted.","Recover axes and scientifically justify branch gates before measuring lengths.","Keep upstream and downstream transport budgets separate; no sum over graph edges.","Review original processing and observation gaps before new derived dimensions."]},"source_sha256":"a857f6be29353bfb10f79fb91f51466049fc3324cd769d56de44af60e1506a0a"},{"note":{"current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","label":"Measurement object scope: passage network","audit_file":"research/current-measurement-scopes/indonesian-throughflow.json","summary":"Measure each passage with explicit depth, period and boundary rules. Channel and transport-integration spans are not current-width boundaries.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_locator":"Existing cited current ledger entry and explicit component links; retained source-scope audit research/indonesian-throughflow-network-scope-audit.json","observed_period":null,"measurement_scope_assessment":true,"related_current_ids":[],"related_proposed_current_ids":[]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-measurement-object-scope.v1","current_id":"indonesian-throughflow","name":"Indonesian Throughflow","status":"editorial_measurement_scope_assessment_not_physical_taxonomy_admission","scope_kind":"passage_network","summary":"Measure each passage with explicit depth, period and boundary rules. Channel and transport-integration spans are not current-width boundaries.","members":[],"source_registry_file":"research/current-measurement-object-scope-index.json","basis_object_sha256":"6f438c549817bd4f0099f727b6244b62fc99ad4a9607e1f3ed1bc89f655e360e","generator_file":"analysis/build_current_measurement_scopes.py","generator_sha256":"1357a690e4780eff266db7e95c1998498df88f1e76fdff570b2676d78528534f","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008JC005257","source_locator":"Existing cited cu