/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=3357","candidate_ids":["ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"Northern Current segment","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The source describes a Northern Current formed in the Ligurian Sea that flows onward along the Provençal and Balearic slopes; the Ligurian name is treated here as its source-region segment, without assigning the whole system's extent to this record.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"ligurian","label":"Ligurian studied segment within Northern Current","audit_file":"research/ligurian-northern-segment-scope-audit.json","summary":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow. Surface sampled Genoaâ€“Menton/Nice reach retains editorial gates. Local 15â€“35 km offshore profile band supplies approximately 20 km span; no whole-current or seasonal width inferred.","source_url":"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf","source_locator":"Poulain et al. (2012), Introduction pp. 261â€“263: NC formation and Italian/French coastal continuation; sections 2.1 and 4, pp. 264â€“266 and 274â€“276: surface sampling, Genoa, Imperia, Mentonâ€“Nice and current structure.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"ligurian","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf","source_access":"primary_pdf_relevant_sections_read","source_citation":"Poulain, Gerin, Rixen, Zanasca, Teixeira, Griffa, Molcard, de Marte and Pinardi (2012), Aspects of the surface circulation in the Liguro-Provencal basin and Gulf of Lion as observed by satellite-tracked drifters (2007–2009), Bollettino di Geofisica Teorica ed Applicata 53(2), 261–279, doi:10.4430/bgta0052.","declared_reach_gates":{"upstream":[8.95,44.1],"downstream":[7.35,43.5],"role":"editorial_neighborhood_truncations_not_formal_named_current_endpoints"},"parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","parent_scope_note":"The ledger treats Ligurian Current as a Northern Current segment. This studied reach overlaps the broader current geography; do not add its length to the parent or count it as an independent parallel flow.","naming_reference":{"url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=3357","mrgid":3357,"status":"Proposed standard","endpoint_geometry_present":false,"does_not_establish_osw_segment_convention":true},"layer":"Surface-flow geography in a study combining CODE drifters following the first metre and ARGOSPHERE drifters following the first 10–20 cm with unquantified wind slip. No full-depth or shelf-break axis diagnosed from the editorial route.","sampling_context":"Source drifter sampling is intermittent during May–October 2007 and October 2008–January 2009. The selected reach is editorial geographic context, not one float trajectory, simultaneous observation, annual mean or seasonal path.","observed_period":null,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"additional_width_evidence_pending_definition_review":{"source_locator":"Section 4, p. 274 and Discussion p. 276; Fig. 9","imperia_coast_distance_limit_range_km":[20,30],"interpretation":"Imperia coast-to-limit range remains unresolved as a width metric. Menton–Nice band is now separately extracted as a local approximately 20 km profile-band span, not paired whole-current width or seasonal margin.","numeric_inventory_admission":false},"excluded_inferences":["No basin-wide recirculation loops added to coastal reach length.","No Corsica feeder path or upstream formation location treated as this gate.","No winter/summer parent widths transferred to local segment.","No broad paper sampling window treated as a continuously observed route."],"remaining_gates":["Resolve the geographic Ligurian naming convention before whole-segment endpoint admission.","Review source sampling/layer and coastal path with finer bathymetry or compatible current data.","Keep overlapping Northern Current and Ligurian segment lengths separate; do not sum them.","Review local 20 km Menton–Nice profile-band extraction, mixed surface support and remaining Imperia coast-distance limit; no paired whole-current width inferred."],"profile_band_width_extraction":{"measurement_id":"ligurian-menton-nice-composite-profile-band","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","source_current_label":"Northern Current","source_parent_current_id":"northern-mediterranean","source_reported_band_limits_km":[15,35],"approximate_local_span_km":20,"span_calculation":"farther_minus_nearer_coast_distance","full_width_inference_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false}},"source_sha256":"ec5a47eb140325d566f4513266d9498813bb0e0a266e32189cd7c4ff516b85c4"}]},{"id":"route-decision:loop","entity_id":"current:loop","label":"Loop Current","current_id":"loop","strategy_id":"dated_geometry","strategy_label":"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Review regional gateway placement, effective resolution and original maximum-velocity contour details against five dated NOAA/DUACS comparisons. Four predeclared 2025 dates retain three failed nominal NOAA traces, while DUACS remains connected. Assess broader observed regimes; failed methods and sparse snapshots do not establish annual ranges. See research/loop-current-recorded-date-comparison.json; no ranked length or width admitted.","scope":"The loop expands and retracts; its path length changes.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/loopcurrent.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"loop","name":"Loop Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The loop expands and retracts; its path length changes.","name_source_url":"https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/loopcurrent.html","candidate_ids":[],"reference_path_decision":"reference_path_not_constructed","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"western boundary current segment","route_strategy_id":"dated_geometry","route_strategy_label":"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The loop expands and retracts; its path length changes.","next_action":"Review regional gateway placement, effective resolution and original maximum-velocity contour details against five dated NOAA/DUACS comparisons. Four predeclared 2025 dates retain three failed nominal NOAA traces, while DUACS remains connected. Assess broader observed regimes; failed methods and sparse snapshots do not establish annual ranges. See research/loop-current-recorded-date-comparison.json; no ranked length or width admitted.","strategy_next_action":"Use dated or explicitly averaged geometry, distinguish an open loop from a closed circuit, and compare repeated regimes before summarizing.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"loop","label":"Dated open-path methods and ADT comparison","audit_file":"research/loop-current-altimetry-method-scope-audit.json","summary":"Five dated NOAA/DUACS comparisons are retained. For four predeclared 2025 dates, NOAA connects only in April; its other nominal traces stop at missing velocities. DUACS supplies four contours; April method difference is 19.5 km. The September 2026 comparison and failed neighbors remain available. Shared inputs, gates and sparse date coverage prevent treating these as independent confirmation, annual extrema, widths or ranked whole-current lengths.","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159/full","source_locator":"Sections 2.2, 3.1 and 4.1; local pinned 25 September 2026 experiments","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"loop","as_of":"2026-10-04","status":"editorial_source_and_diagnostic_summary_not_canonical","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159/full","source_citation":"Manta et al. (2023), Predicting the Loop Current dynamics combining altimetry and deep flow measurements through the Yucatan Channel, Frontiers in Marine Science 10:1156159, doi:10.3389/fmars.2023.1156159.","source_access":"Full publisher HTML methods and results read. Figures were not digitized. Supplemental numerical Loop Current paths were not acquired.","source_locators":["Sections 2.2, 3.1, 4.1; Figures 1C and 2A captions"],"observed_period":{"start_year":1993,"end_year":2021,"exact_endpoint_days":null},"source_product":"Copernicus DUACS DT-2018 daily 0.25-degree absolute dynamic topography and surface geostrophic velocity","published_metrics":[{"method":"Demeaned 0.17 m sea-level contour connecting Yucatan Channel and Florida Straits","mean_extension_km":1449,"standard_deviation_km":487,"is_confidence_interval":false,"is_length_of_temporal_mean_path":false},{"method":"Maximum-geostrophic-velocity streamline connecting Yucatan Channel and Florida Straits","mean_extension_km":1495,"standard_deviation_km":466,"is_confidence_interval":false,"is_length_of_temporal_mean_path":false}],"method_comparison":{"correlation":0.86,"root_mean_square_difference_km":262},"range_interpretation":"Source describes retracted states below 1000 km and extended phases around 1800–2600 km. These are phase descriptions, not an annual extrema range, confidence interval or width.","diagnostic_file":"research/loop-current-dated-streamline-20260925.json","diagnostic_page":"almanac/loop-current-experiment.html","comparison_diagnostic_file":"research/loop-current-adt-contours-20260925.json","comparison_source_file":"research/gcoos-duacs-loop-20260925.json","comparison_result":"Highest length-weighted mean speed among 31 eligible gateway-connected ADT contours occurs at 0.62 m ADT. Selected path rounds to 2200 km and is 55.9 km shorter than the NOAA trace before display rounding. This is product/method disagreement, not independent observation, uncertainty or a physical range.","diagnostic_observation_date":"2026-09-25","diagnostic_method":"OSW frozen-time velocity integration with strongest northward native-grid seed at an editorial regional gate; distinct from both source contour algorithms","diagnostic_source_product":"NOAA LSA RADS 4.8.1 Experimental daily absolute surface geostrophic velocities; lacks absolute dynamic topography","diagnostic_result":"Nominal gateway-connected path rounds to 2300 km; all four neighboring seed scenarios fail. Integration step changes are small, but no robust range follows from only successful tests.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"rank_eligible":false,"remaining_gates":["Validate gateway placement and section alternatives using geographic and bathymetric evidence","Compatible same-date DUACS ADT acquired through GCOOS; recover original supplemental maximum-velocity algorithm and compare its gateway/method choices","Preserve failed seed outcomes and assess effective resolution and grid masks","Four predeclared dates tested; assess original method/gateway choices and broader repeated-date coverage before describing physical variability or seasonal ranges","Complete scientific and regional raw-subset source-use review before admission/publication"],"recorded_date_comparison_file":"research/loop-current-recorded-date-comparison.json","recorded_date_page":"almanac/loop-current-recorded-dates.html","recorded_date_result":"Predeclared 15 January, April, July and October 2025 snapshots: NOAA connects only on April 15 (1573.2 km), failing at missing velocity on three dates. DUACS selects contours on all four dates (2082.9, 1592.7, 1674.0, 989.4 km); April difference 19.5 km. Four recorded days are not annual extrema, phase labels or a climatology. Preserve product/method failures."},"source_sha256":"807d7901af9483625b6d3074d7edefcf46b410284217c5a1f7a99f60c4a36d7f"}]},{"id":"route-decision:mauritanian","entity_id":"current:mauritanian","label":"Mauritanian Current","current_id":"mauritanian","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["mauritanian-summer-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The source reports poleward surface flow during the May–July relaxation season in the Mauritanian upwelling region; winter upwelling-season coastal flow is equatorward. A single year-round direction or whole-current length would misrepresent this seasonal regime.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=30081","source_decision":{"current_id":"mauritanian","name":"Mauritanian Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The source reports poleward surface flow during the May–July relaxation season in the Mauritanian upwelling region; winter upwelling-season coastal flow is equatorward. A single year-round direction or whole-current length would misrepresent this seasonal regime.","name_source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=30081","candidate_ids":["mauritanian-summer-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"seasonal poleward eastern-boundary current","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The source reports poleward surface flow during the May–July relaxation season in the Mauritanian upwelling region; winter upwelling-season coastal flow is equatorward. A single year-round direction or whole-current length would misrepresent this seasonal regime.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"mauritanian","label":"Poleward surface/undercurrent manifestations and seasonal mean width","audit_file":"research/mauritanian-seasonal-mean-scope-audit.json","summary":"At reference 18 N, the study names poleward surface and subsurface manifestations Mauritania Current. Its 30–40 km upwelling-season mean undercurrent width is local; the equatorward shelf jet, transport window and broader surface corridor are separate. No whole-current route or annual width range established.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014264","source_locator":"Sections 2.1, 3.1, 4 and 5; Table 2 and Figure 5 caption.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"mauritanian","status":"editorial_source_scope_not_scientific_approval","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014264","source_access":"Publisher Introduction, section 2.1/Table 2, section 3.1/Figures 4–5 captions, Discussion and Conclusion read. No figure digitization, raw fields or underlying cruise reports acquired.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-03","scope":"Reference 18 N seasonal mean section; local measurements pooled from 17–19 N via reference topography.","width_record_id":"mauritanian-upwelling-seasonal-mean-width-range","source_naming_rule":"Authors propose Mauritania Current for both poleward surface and undercurrent manifestations. Equatorward shelf surface flow is a separate opposing feature, not a reversal of the entire named poleward flow.","upwelling_season_months":[12,1,2,3,4],"relaxation_season_months":[5,6,7],"excluded_cruise":"M129 August 2016 excluded from both means","source_width_range_km":[30,40],"width_role":"author_reported_span_of_upwelling_season_mean_undercurrent","width_edges_extracted":false,"fixed_depth_width":false,"transport_window_is_width":false,"surface_200_km_context_is_width":false,"source_conflict":"Introduction cites Kounta coastal-wave passage to 20 S despite northward context; not interpreted as a geographic current endpoint.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"observed_period":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"remaining_gates":["Recover layer-compatible paired edges and field axes with sampling support.","Resolve along-coast and relaxation-season dimensions; preserve annual gaps.","Independent scientific identity/measurement admission."]},"source_sha256":"ec077cf15908d66b9520089a2714f1550a2796c160a9f8415868129c17ca53f6"}]},{"id":"route-decision:mediterranean-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:mediterranean-undercurrent","label":"Mediterranean Undercurrent","current_id":"mediterranean-undercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["mediterranean-undercurrent-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"RAFOS floats and hydrography track the undercurrent from the Gulf of Cádiz around southwestern Portugal, where a roughly 30 km wide jet weakens and broadens northward. That width is cross-stream, not its length; branching and loss from the slope prevent a single measured endpoint here.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2001JC001007","source_decision":{"current_id":"mediterranean-undercurrent","name":"Mediterranean Undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"RAFOS floats and hydrography track the undercurrent from the Gulf of Cádiz around southwestern Portugal, where a roughly 30 km wide jet weakens and broadens northward. That width is cross-stream, not its length; branching and loss from the slope prevent a single measured endpoint here.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2001JC001007","candidate_ids":["mediterranean-undercurrent-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"intermediate-depth boundary undercurrent","route_strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","route_strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"RAFOS floats and hydrography track the undercurrent from the Gulf of Cádiz around southwestern Portugal, where a roughly 30 km wide jet weakens and broadens northward. That width is cross-stream, not its length; branching and loss from the slope prevent a single measured endpoint here.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"mediterranean-undercurrent","label":"Lower-core studied reach versus broader Mediterranean Water spreading","audit_file":"research/mediterranean-undercurrent-layer-branch-scope-audit.json","summary":"AMUSE lower-core reach around Cape St. Vincent remains separate from Gibraltar density flow, offshore water spreading and meddy loops. Regional 30 km and 10 km width metrics do not form a seasonal range; whole-current endpoints unresolved.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2001JC001007","source_locator":"Data [7]; Results 3.2â€“3.3 [19]â€“[25].","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"mediterranean-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2001JC001007","source_access":"full_primary_publisher_page_read","source_citation":"Bower, Serra and Ambar (2002), Structure of the Mediterranean Undercurrent and Mediterranean Water spreading around the southwestern Iberian Peninsula, JGR Oceans 107(C10), doi:10.1029/2001JC001007.","declared_reach_gates":{"upstream":[-8.5,36.5],"downstream":[-9.65,38.2],"role":"AMUSE_context_to_editorial_western_slope_truncation_not_whole_current_endpoints"},"layer":"Nonmeddy lower-core Mediterranean Water context, 950–1250 dbar observational selection. Pressure bounds are not converted to uniform depth; vertically separated cores and upstream bottom-trapped density flow remain distinct.","observed_period":null,"sampling_context":"AMUSE floats deployed May 1993–March 1994 and tracked for up to 11 months, with May 1993 hydrography and augmented Iberian observations. Selected path is editorial geography, not one dated float trajectory, annual mean or seasonal axis.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_dimension_ranges":null,"width_scope":"30 km core-to-offshore zero crossing and 10 km geostrophic survey band have different boundaries and support; not a seasonal pair.","additional_width_evidence_pending_definition_review":{"source_locator":"Results 3.2 [22]","reported_lower_bound_km":50,"feature":"Mean northward-flow band in western slope Region 2, 0.04–0.06 m/s; source says at least 50 km, not a paired-edge whole-current width.","numeric_inventory_admission":false},"excluded_inferences":["No upstream gravity-current route silently joined to lower core.","No salt-tongue geometry equated with current axis.","No meddy float loops counted in boundary-current length.","No float launch window treated as observation end dates."],"remaining_gates":["Review launch neighborhood, cape detour and 38.2 N longitude against finer bathymetry and observational support.","Diagnose a depth/time-compatible current axis before physical length or seasonal bounds.","Resolve western-slope branch loss and farther-north continuity before whole-current endpoints.","Keep 30 km one-sided ensemble span and 10 km survey band separate; no seasonal 10–30 km width range or buffered footprint."]},"source_sha256":"4f71a744f40022a2de29b70f70d0ddc4b6eb789762b696b28f4cb23e71e5a84f"}]},{"id":"route-decision:mindanao-current","entity_id":"current:mindanao-current","label":"Mindanao Current","current_id":"mindanao-current","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["mindanao-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The source describes flow southward along the Philippine Islands and supply to the Indonesian Throughflow, North Equatorial Countercurrent, and Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent. It gives no whole-current alongflow length or fixed endpoint gates.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_decision":{"current_id":"mindanao-current","name":"Mindanao Current","existi