ranch fitted scale versus whole North Cape system","audit_file":"research/north-cape-branch-profile-scope-audit.json","summary":"2007 observations support an approximately 8 km Northern-branch Gaussian profile scale, not paired-edge full width or a seasonal range. Whole-system route and dimensions remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://physical-oceanography.ru/repository/issues/2017/02/05/20170205.pdf","source_locator":"Stationary currents p. 38; Currents pp. 45â€“47, Fig. 10 and fitted-profile paragraph.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"north-cape","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://physical-oceanography.ru/repository/issues/2017/02/05/20170205.pdf","source_access":"full_primary_pdf_read","doi":"10.22449/1573-160X-2017-2-36-50","branch_scope":"Northern branch, distinct from Central branch; partial cyclonic recirculation described, not a single whole-system axis.","numeric_evidence":{"record_id":"north-cape-northern-2007-profile-scale","source_effective_width_km":8,"crossing_count":15,"metric_interpretation":"OSW center-to-e-folding inference from the published Gaussian formula","full_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null},"temporal_scope":{"composite_description":"summer expeditions of 2007","exact_composite_dates":null,"described_cruise":{"start":"2007-05-29","end":"2007-06-10"},"figure_1_track_label":{"start":"2007-05-30","end":"2007-06-09"},"dates_are_not_interchangeable":true},"layer_scope":"Composite vertical support unresolved. Fig. 9 specifies a 20–80 m average for LS05; Fig. 10 does not explicitly establish that same fixed layer for all 15 crossings. Instrument generally sampled from about 20 m to 150 m or 15 m above bottom.","excluded_inferences":["Do not use the 0.5 km thermal-front scale as current width.","Do not transfer LS05 20–80 m averaging to all Fig. 10 crossings.","Do not turn BarKode annual salinity variability into annual current width.","Do not admit doubled e-folding span or Gaussian FWHM as sourced widths."],"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"route_geometry":null,"remaining_gates":["Resolve exact composite depth averaging and crossing dates from underlying data.","Define comparable paired boundaries before any full-width comparison.","Review branch identity and along-route support; canonical admission remains pending."],"source_document_sha256":"76cdf260067540a0102d7f40d5f1220f7e6f3884f7f543d4deda6bef77612eaf","source_figures_inspected":["Fig. 1 PDF page 2","Fig. 9 PDF page 11"],"route_context_note":"Western Hopen Northern-branch studied reach has OSW-selected gates, distinct from full current system and transverse LS05 ship track."},"source_sha256":"68eb7e1aa063d2cdf736ac1470387d94b78096f2c87981edfb71fac1d051dc02"}]},{"id":"route-decision:north-equatorial-countercurrent","entity_id":"current:north-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"North Equatorial Countercurrent","current_id":"north-equatorial-countercurrent","strategy_id":"split_basin_family","strategy_label":"Split basin families","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.","scope":"Atlantic and Pacific upper-ocean currents share a name but have distinct paths and seasonality. The family has no single measured length; this is distinct from the deeper North Equatorial Undercurrent.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=5387","source_decision":{"current_id":"north-equatorial-countercurrent","name":"North Equatorial Countercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Atlantic and Pacific upper-ocean currents share a name but have distinct paths and seasonality.