 PDF7; Figure4 caption on the same page. Figure1 printed571 / PDF3 provides branch and sampling context.","scope":"REDSOX northern descending plume reach; channel branches precede equilibrated-water spreading.","reported_reach":{"approximate_length_km":130,"length_metric":"author_reported_winter_velocity_supported_descending_plume_reach","branch_id":"redsox-northern-channel-plume","origin_label":"Bab el Mandeb","source_velocity_quantity":"plume_speed_magnitude","velocity_threshold_m_s":0.2,"threshold_operator":">","layer_thickness_range_m":[100,250],"fixed_depth_bounds_m":null,"campaign_context":{"source":"Peters et al. Table 1","start":"2001-02-11","end":"2001-03-15","is_exact_reach_sampling_period":false},"observed_period":null,"is_synoptic_snapshot":false,"geometry":null,"length_range_km":null,"rank_eligible":false,"whole_current_representative":false},"branches":[{"id":"redsox-northern-channel-plume","label":"Northern Channel plume","parent_component":"red-sea-saline-overflow","component_role":"descending_plume_branch","canonical_identity":false,"geometry":null,"whole_branch_length_km":null,"width_km":null},{"id":"redsox-southern-channel-main-plume","label":"Southern Channel main plume","parent_component":"red-sea-saline-overflow","component_role":"descending_plume_branch","canonical_identity":false,"geometry":null,"whole_branch_length_km":null,"width_km":null},{"id":"redsox-southern-channel-gully-plume","label":"Southern Channel gully product","parent_component":"redsox-southern-channel-main-plume","component_role":"winter_product_water_branch","canonical_identity":false,"geometry":null,"whole_branch_length_km":null,"width_km":null}],"channel_dimension_context":[{"source":"Peters et al. abstract","approximate_length_km":130,"approximate_width_km":5,"metric":"bathymetric_northern_channel_description"},{"source":"Peters et al. section 3a","approximate_length_km":120,"approximate_width_km":5,"metric":"confined_northern_channel_path_description"},{"source":"Bower et al. section 3a","approximate_length_km":115,"approximate_width_km":5,"metric":"bathymetric_northern_channel_description"}],"channel_values_are_current_dimensions":false,"channel_value_spread_is_uncertainty_interval":false,"source_consistency_note":"Channel length conventions remain unresolved; no range formed from differing descriptions. Bower cruise context starts February 5; Peters Table 1 starts February 11.","downstream_continuity_note":"Bower et al. found no continuous boundary undercurrent in these observations; equilibrated water and descending branches remain distinct.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Bower_etal_2005_EquilibrationCirculation.pdf","locator":"Sections 2, 3a-b; Table 1; abstract","citation":"Bower et al. (2005), doi:10.1175/JPO2787.1"}],"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"remaining_gates":["Recover compatible current axes and paired velocity boundaries.","Resolve channel conventions and exact occupation support.","Independent branch identity and measurement admission."]},"source_sha256":"d54695661b969a6f2a7b5f99c95c3097b2fa111f2dc24a941f082efa8ab758b0"}]},{"id":"route-decision:solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","entity_id":"current:solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","label":"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent","current_id":"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The source schematically names this equatorward flow along the Solomon Islands and says it may feed the New Ireland Coastal Undercurrent. Its continuity and whole-current length are unresolved.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","source_decision":{"current_id":"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","name":"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The source schematically names this equatorward flow along the Solomon Islands and says it may feed the New Ireland Coastal Undercurrent. Its continuity and whole-current length are unresolved.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1029/2011JC007477","candidate_ids":["solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"proposed subsurface island boundary current","route_strategy_id":"layer_specific_route","route_strategy_label":"Construct layer-specific paths","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The source schematically names this equatorward flow along the Solomon Islands and says it may feed the New Ireland Coastal Undercurrent. Its continuity and whole-current length are unresolved.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","label":"Model proposal, later regional observations and editorial reach","audit_file":"research/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-proposal-scope-audit.json","summary":"The 2010 model proposes SICU east of the Solomon Islands. A pinned 2017 primary paper interprets northward flow near northeast Bougainville, with ADCP and tracer station context. OSW adds an offshore geographic reference reach; continuous measured axis, complete endpoints, width and annual ranges remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html","source_locator":"Author-hosted abstract: previously unknown current east of Solomon Sea formed where SEC meets Solomon Islands; named Solomon Islands Coastal Undercurrent.","observed_period":null,"supporting_sources":[{"label":"Ganachaud et al. (2017), Solomon Sea cruises","url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221","locator":"Figures 2 and 7; pages 5-7, 11-12 and 17","access":"Original NOAA-hosted PDF acquired and institutional SHA256 matched; CC BY 4.0 printed page 27; selected pages and figures inspected."}]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent","as_of":"2026-10-09","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html","source_citation":"Melet, Gourdeau, Kessler, Verron and Molines (2010), Thermocline circulation in the Solomon Sea: A modeling study, J. Phys. Oceanogr. 40, 1302–1319, doi:10.1175/2009JPO4264.1.","source_access":"Melet et al. (2010) coauthor-hosted abstract read; indexed primary text provides additional model context but the original full article remains inaccessible. Ganachaud et al. (2017) original 27-page PDF acquired from NOAA, checksum matched to institutional record; relevant methods, figures and SICU discussion inspected. No velocity field or source axis digitized.","source_locator":"Author-hosted abstract: previously unknown current east of Solomon Sea formed where SEC meets Solomon Islands; named Solomon Islands Coastal Undercurrent.","source_name":"Solomon Islands Coastal Undercurrent","ledger_name":"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent","name_scope_decision":"Plural spelling is the source label; no canonical alias mutation in this audit.","flow_evidence_class":"modeled_proposal_with_later_regional_observational_interpretation","source_model_resolution_degrees":0.08333333333333333,"source_model_resolution_is_route_precision":false,"scope":"Equatorward boundary flow on the Pacific side of the Solomon Islands proposed in the 2010 model. The 2017 paper interprets northward SICU flow near northeast Bougainville using Pandora ADCP and Al/Mn station contrasts. Neither the abstract nor these local observations establishes a measured continuous island-chain axis, complete endpoints or whole-current dimensions.","observed_period":null,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"editorial_regional_geographic_reach_available_continuity_unresolved","remaining_gates":["Acquire and visually review the original 2010 model Figure 4 before digitizing a model axis.","Review finer coastline and bathymetry, source velocity fields and the density-dependent flow before identifying an actual current core.","Resolve complete entrance/exit gates and connectivity to NICU separately; no connector across Solomon Strait is drawn.","No whole-current width, annual range, dated footprint or NASA surface identification inferred."],"source_document_file":"research/source-data/ganachaud-solomon-2017/journal-article.pdf","source_document_sha256":"981f64dfa09125766a185228391a4e8099f98285cedaaaedecccc9533fa03b9e","acquisition_file":"research/source-data/ganachaud-solomon-2017/acquisition.json","acquisition_sha256":"938ba5c93669ea72a390046bd9bc00e922605b1c7e17ab0212c18428855677d1","evidence_contexts":[{"id":"melet-2010-model-proposal","class":"source_proposed_modeled_flow","source_url":"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html","locator":"Coauthor abstract; indexed primary Figure 4 caption and mean thermocline discussion","layer":"Model thermocline sigma 24.0-26.5; roughly 100-400 m but density layer varies in depth, not a fixed depth slab","time":"1986-2004 model mean, from indexed Figure 4 caption; not an observation period","access":"Abstract and indexed excerpts; original full article and Figure 4 not acquired or visually reviewed","continuity_observed":false},{"id":"ganachaud-2017-pandora-interpretation","class":"regional_observational_interpretation","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221","locator":"Pages 5-7 methods and cruise context; Figure 7 and pages 11-12; page 17 Al/Mn discussion","campaign_voyage_dates":["2012-06-28","2012-08-06"],"current_axis_observation_dates":null,"layer":"Figure 7c shipboard ADCP layers 0-100 m and 100-300 m are separate from the model density layer; page 17 does not define an SICU core depth","finding":"The source interprets northward SICU flow near station 43 northeast of Bougainville. Station 42 in Solomon Strait differs from station 43; reported ADCP shows no flow between those adjacent sites. Similarities to station 13 do not prove a continuous axis.","continuity_observed":false},{"id":"ganachaud-2017-surface-context","class":"surface_context_not_undercurrent_geometry","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221","locator":"Figure 7 caption and page 12 ocean circulation","finding":"Northwestward surface flow near the east Bougainville coast is associated with cyclonic circulation. Figure 7a/b combines campaign mean altimetric anomalies with GDP 1979-March 2015 annual mean climatology; Figure 7c/d is cruise shipboard ADCP. These operators are not interchangeable.","whole_undercurrent_geometry":false}],"reference_route_role":"OSW editorial offshore island-chain geography, not a traced model streamline or continuous observed axis","rank_eligible":false,"seasonal_playback_eligible":false},"source_sha256":"476ab173d565d7741cadf354abb3ef981b20c3b3c9c2f9d27d80f5d0ea408586"}]},{"id":"route-decision:somali","entity_id":"current:somali","label":"Somali Current","current_id":"somali","strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":2,"route_ids":["somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate","somali-winter-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"Seasonal reversal makes a single static length misleading.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"somali","name":"Somali Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Seasonal reversal makes a single static length misleading.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":["somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate","somali-winter-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"monsoon-reversing current","route_strategy_id":"seasonal_routes","route_strategy_label":"Construct seasonal routes","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"Seasonal reversal makes a single static length misleading.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Choose sourced season, direction and 