rrent path length admitted. Do not conflate with the Agulhas Return Current or offshore West Australian Current. Cartographic crossings remain separately pending review.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2014gb004898","source_decision":{"current_id":"south-indian","name":"South Indian Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Eastward subtropical-gyre flow near 40 degrees S in the cited study; no source-defined whole-current path length admitted. Do not conflate with the Agulhas Return Current or offshore West Australian Current. Cartographic crossings remain separately pending review.","name_source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2014gb004898","candidate_ids":["south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"basin-spanning current","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"Eastward subtropical-gyre flow near 40 degrees S in the cited study; no source-defined whole-current path length admitted. Do not conflate with the Agulhas Return Current or offshore West Australian Current. Cartographic crossings remain separately pending review.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"south-indian","label":"Eastern naming convention and idealized transport reach","audit_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-naming-layer-scope-audit.json","summary":"70–90 E is a declared regional reach under the eastern SIOC naming convention. Longitude gates are approximate context, and every latitude/connecting bend is editorial. Historical upper-1000 m transport is not a fixed-depth axis; western ARC, recirculation and northeastern continuation are not summed. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455","source_locator":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997) section 3.2; Grand et al. (2015) section 3.1.1; earlier/later naming conventions retained.","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["agulhas-return"]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"south-indian","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455","source_citation":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), The flow field of the subtropical gyre of the South Indian Ocean, JGR 102, 5513–5530, doi:10.1029/96JC03455.","source_locator":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997), section 3.2 / journal p. 5523 and Figure 7 caption: 90 E recirculation/split and upper-1000 m flow schematic. Later Grand et al. (2015), regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113: SIOC name beyond 70 E. Near-40 S context from Stramma (1992) publisher abstract; drawn latitudes are editorial.","source_access":"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997) PDF Introduction, Methods and section 3.2 / Figure 7 caption read; Grand et al. (2015) PDF section 3.1.1 read. Stramma (1992) publisher abstract read. Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001) publisher-indexed abstract available; direct publisher page returned 403. No source figure or field digitized.","scope":"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.","layer":"Historical upper-1000 m geostrophic transport context, not a uniform-depth velocity axis or surface trajectory. Variable deep reference surfaces affect diagnosed transport; no layer-specific centerline reconstructed.","time_convention":"Editorial regional connection informed by historical hydrographic mean-flow context and source naming conventions. Not a simultaneous observation, monthly climatological axis or annual geometry.","observed_period":null,"naming_conventions":[{"source":"Stramma (1992); Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997)","extent_convention":"Broad eastward southern-gyre flow, including western transport context.","physical_endpoints_established":false},{"source":"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001); Grand et al. (2015)","extent_convention":"Retain SIOC name beyond ARC termination near 66–70 E; eastern regional flow weak/dispersed.","physical_endpoints_established":false}],"name_equivalence_status":"Source-convention interpretation under existing South Indian ledger record; no universal alias equivalence established.","longitude_gates_are_exact_physical_junctions":false,"latitudes_are_editorial":true,"upper_1000m_transport_is_uniform_axis_layer":false,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","input_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-input.json","candidate_file":"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":1700,"reported_scenario_range_km":[1600,1800],"scenario_count":27,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false},"supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/abstract/journals/phoc/22/4/1520-0485_1992_022_0421_tsioc_2_0_co_2.xml","citation":"Stramma (1992), The South Indian Ocean Current, JPO 22, 421–430.","locator":"Publisher abstract only: near-40 S STF context and eastern separation beyond 100 E.","supports":"Broad earlier current name and approximate frontal geography; no source centerline digitized."},{"url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796301000410","citation":"Lutjeharms and Ansorge (2001), The Agulhas Return Current, Journal of Marine Systems 30, 115–138.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct publisher retrieval returned 403.","supports":"Proposed ARC termination near 66–70 E and SIOC name farther east; source convention, not fixed physical junction."},{"url":"https://science.whoi.edu/users/mcgillic/cruises/TN376/cruiseshare/Morton%20lab/Relevant%20Papers/Grand%20et%20al.%20-%202015%20-%20The%20impact%20of%20circulation%20and%20dust%20deposition%20in%20controlling%20the%20distributions%20of%20dissolved%20Fe%20and%20Al%20in%20the%20south.pdf","citation":"Grand et al. (2015), The impact of circulation and dust deposition in controlling the distributions of dissolved Fe and Al in the south Indian subtropical gyre, Marine Chemistry 176, 110–125.","locator":"Regional circulation discussion, journal p. 113 / PDF page 4.","supports":"SIOC name beyond 70 E; near-90 E recirculation and dispersed eastern flow."}],"remaining_gates":["Review the longitude naming transition and exact regional layer against compatible velocity fields.","Resolve the distinction among South Indian Current, South Indian Ocean Current and Agulhas Return under each source convention.","Diagnose meanders and local latitude shifts; the near-40 S editorial connection is not an observed axis.","Resolve the 90 E branching and northeastern continuation independently before any whole-current length.","Recover matching seasonal axes and transverse boundaries before annual length/width ranges."]},"source_sha256":"0321bf4f204390217073f2e6d319e37e04e4f9dbd3a23e555a76a17a80c0919e"}]},{"id":"route-decision:south-pacific","entity_id":"current:south-pacific","label":"South Pacific Current","current_id":"south-pacific","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"Named eastward current associated with the South Pacific subtropical front; map arrows do not measure its full length.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml","source_decision":{"current_id":"south-pacific","name":"South Pacific Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"Named eastward current associated with the South Pacific subtropical front; map arrows do not measure its full length.","name_source_url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml","candidate_ids":["south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"basin-spanning current","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"Named eastward current associated with the South Pacific subtropical front; map arrows do not measure its full length.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"south-pacific","label":"Frontal proxies, separate-year sections and layered flow","audit_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-layer-time-scope-audit.json","summary":"The 103–88 W studied reach connects reported STF crossings sampled in 1994 and 1993. Frontal proxies are not velocity cores or simultaneous geometry. The 150 m temperature criterion does not define an axis depth; branch correspondence and whole-current dimensions remain unresolved. Layered gyre flow cannot be identified universally by the STF.","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [5], Table 1 and STF [14]–[17]; Ridgway and Dunn (2007), section 3.4 [15].","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"south-pacific","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf","source_citation":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Surface circulation and fronts of the South Pacific Ocean, east of 120 W, Geophysical Research Letters 32, L08605, doi:10.1029/2004GL022070.","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Data [4]–[5], surface circulation [7], STF [14]–[17] and Table 1: P18 at 103 W 33.8 S and P19 at 88 W 34.5 S. Source front/velocity distinction retained; fields and curves not digitized.","source_access":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005) repository PDF Data, sections 3.1–3.3, Table 1 text and summary read. Stramma et al. (1995) publisher-indexed abstract read; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful. Ridgway and Dunn (2007) publisher section 3.4 [15] read. No figure/velocity curve digitized.","scope":"Declared 103 W to 88 W eastern regional studied reach between two reported Subtropical Front crossings associated with the SPC in the source regional surface circulation. Front locations are proxies, not diagnosed velocity-core endpoints, and were observed in different years. OSW connecting vertices and alternatives are editorial. Branch correspondence is unresolved. Excludes Chatham Rise/western basin, ACC export branch, Peru-Chile coastal flow, northward recirculation and independent split bands. Not a whole-current or simultaneous observed axis.","layer":"Surface drifter circulation context combined with separate hydrographic STF crossing locations. The 14 C at 150 m frontal criterion does not define a 150 m current axis; drifter velocities include ageostrophic flow. No fixed-depth velocity centerline reconstructed.","time_convention":"1979–2004 regional drifter mean is context; P18 frontal crossing was sampled February–April 1994 and P19 February–April 1993. This editorial connection does not combine them into one dated trajectory or infer seasonal geometry.","observed_period":null,"source_anchor_observations":[{"id":"p18-1994-stf-crossing","longitude_latitude":[-103,-33.8],"observed_period":{"start":"1994-02","end":"1994-04"},"time_precision":"month","geometry_role":"observed_front_crossing_not_current_axis","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Table 1 / Data [5]: P18 103 W 33.8 S."},{"id":"p19-1993-stf-crossing","longitude_latitude":[-88,-34.5],"observed_period":{"start":"1993-02","end":"1993-04"},"time_precision":"month","geometry_role":"observed_front_crossing_not_current_axis","source_locator":"Chaigneau and Pizarro (2005), Table 1 / Data [5]: P19 88 W 34.5 S."}],"frontal_crossings_are_velocity_core_locations":false,"source_150m_temperature_criterion_is_axis_layer":false,"crossings_form_simultaneous_geometry":false,"branch_correspondence":"unresolved in the source 115–85 W splitting region","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"editorial_candidate_constructed_not_canonical","input_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-input.json","candidate_file":"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate.json","route_approximation":{"reported_approximate_reference_path_km":1400,"reported_scenario_range_km":[1300,1500],"scenario_count":27,"physical_axis_diagnosed":false},"supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml","citation":"Stramma, Peterson and Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, JPO 25, 77–91.","locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful.","supports":"SPC distinction from ACC, broad Chatham Rise context and possible splitting at 115–85 W. Does not assign a branch to this connection."},{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2007GL030392","citation":"Ridgway and Dunn (2007), Observational evidence for a Southern Hemisphere oceanic supergyre, GRL 34, L13612.","locator":"Section 3.4 [15]: gyre return flow and STF relation.","supports":"Layered gyre return flow is not universally identified by the STF; no whole-current or intermediate-layer axis copied from surface/frontal proxies."}],"remaining_gates":["Diagnose a same-layer velocity axis; frontal proxy locations are not current-core locations.","Recover compatible simultaneous observations before a dated route or seasonal extrema.","Resolve two-band correspondence within the 115–85 W split region described by Stramma et al. (1995).","Test front-to-flow correspondence against the layered supergyre distinction in Ridgway and Dunn (2007).","Resolve western and eastern continuation independently before a whole-current length or annual width."]},"source_sha256":"391b88da4e6660d7ad6ca8d2055333d26dca34b89fac4713720cff3a8112c189"}]},{"id":"route-decision:spitsbergen-atlantic","entity_id":"current:spitsbergen-atlantic","label":"Spitsbergen Atlantic Current","current_id":"spitsbergen-atlantic","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Resolve source naming and branch extent before route construction; no transfer of neighboring current dimensions. See research/spitsbergen-atlantic-naming-branch-scope-audit.json.","scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"spitsbergen-atlantic","name":"Spitsbergen Atlantic Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":[],"reference_path_decision":"reference_path_not_constructed","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"regional current","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","next_action":"Resolve source naming and branch extent before route construction; no transfer of neighboring current dimensions. See research/spitsbergen-atlantic-naming-branch-scope-audit.json.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"spitsbergen-atlantic","label":"Naming convention and Atlantic branch scope","audit_file":"research/spitsbergen-atlantic-naming-branch-scope-audit.json","summary":"NOAA Spitsbergen Atlantic Current describes northwestward flow off southwest Spitsbergen. The modern West Spitsbergen Current is a northward Atlantic-water continuation toward Fram Strait. Regional overlap does not establish identical names, branches or endpoints; no existing West Spitsbergen route length is transferred.","related_current_ids":["west-spitsbergen"],"source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary","source_locator":"Norwegian Current, North Atlantic Current and Spitsbergen Atlantic Current entries.","observed_period":null},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"spitsbergen-atlantic","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary","source_access":"Relevant current glossary entries read; not full glossary read.","source_locator":"Norwegian Current, North Atlantic Current and Spitsbergen Atlantic Current entries.","supporting_sources":[{"url":"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/17/2026/","citation":"Baumann, Skagseth, Ingvaldsen and Mork (2026), Reduced cooling in the Norwegian Atlantic Slope Current: investigating mechanisms of change from 30 years of observations, Ocean Science 22, 17–29, doi:10.5194/os-22-17-2026.","locator":"Introduction: two Atlantic branches and northern bifurcation; sections 2.1–2.1.2: sampling/core criteria.","source_access":"Relevant introduction and methods read.","source_license":"CC BY 4.0"}],"summary":"NOAA Spitsbergen Atlantic Current describes northwestward flow off southwest Spitsbergen. The modern West Spitsbergen Current is a northward Atlantic-water continuation toward Fram Strait. Regional overlap does not establish identical names, branches or endpoints; no existing West Spitsbergen route length is transferred.","related_current_ids":["west-spitsbergen"],"name_equivalence_admitted":false,"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"observed_period":null,"route_construction_status":"identity_scope_unresolved","remaining_gates":["Resolve naming convention using direct source definitions before transferring route geometry.","Retain distinct salinity, layer, branch and temporal scope.","No numeric dimensions, footprint or seasonal cycle inferred from nearby currents."]},"source_sha256":"f7a5c4a81ff9fb408097877b3cc0d2c85c8fd65618bccf3ac82bda09823158db"},{"note":{"current_id":"spitsbergen-atlantic","label":"Measurement object scope: unresolved name","audit_file":"research/current-measurement-scopes/spitsbergen-atlantic.json","summary":"Resolve the source-specific name and branch convention before attaching a width. Related records are not confirmed aliases or members.","source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary","source_locator":"Existing cited current ledger entry and explicit component links; retained source-scope audit research/spitsbergen-atlantic-naming-branch-scope-audit.json","observed_period":null,"measurement_scope_assessment":true,"related_current_ids":["west-spitsbergen"],"related_proposed_current_ids":[]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-measurement-object-scope.v1","current_id":"spitsbergen-atlantic","name":"Spitsbergen Atlantic Current","status":"editorial_measurement_scope_assessment_not_physical_taxonomy_admission","scope_kind":"unresolved_name","summary":"Resolve the source-specific name and branch convention before attaching a width. Related records are not confirmed aliases or members.","members":[{"id":"west-spitsbergen","label":"West Spitsbergen Current","record_status":"released","relationship":"related_name_not_equated","scoped_width_record_count":7,"width_values_inherited_by_parent":false}],"source_registry_file":"research/current-measurement-object-scope-index.json","basis_object_sha256":"9695d941d8f6a08542a74ec3c2948a3278f5c2462d6d7f9089a90fee0388c858","generator_file":"analysis/build_current_measurement_scopes.py","generator_sha256":"1357a690e4780eff266db7e95c1998498df88f1e76fdff570b2676d78528534f","source_url":"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary","source_locator":"Existing cited current ledger entry and explicit component links; retained source-scope audit research/spitsbergen-atlantic-naming-branch-scope-audit.json","source_access":"Existing cited ledger and retained scope evidence reviewed; no new field or original-page extraction claimed.","prior_scope_audit_file":"research/spitsbergen-atlantic-naming-branch-scope-audit.json","prior_width_decision":"width_not_assessed","parent_width_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"new_width_record_admitted":false,"member_measurements_inherited":false,"aliases_resolved":false,"physical_taxonomy_admitted":false,"physical_edge_geometry_admitted":false,"observation_date_inherited":false,"figure":"figures/current-measurement-scopes/spitsbergen-atlantic.svg","figure_alt":"Resolve the source-specific name and branch convention before attaching a width. Related records are not confirmed aliases or members. Relationships only; member measurements are not inherited."},"source_sha256":"b95c44ac827201b7cd8129b8a8cbe1e21090eeda79ba2206973d251ba08223fd"}]},{"id":"route-decision:tasman-front","entity_id":"current:tasman-front","label":"Tasman Front","current_id":"tasman-front","strategy_id":"dated_geometry","strategy_label":"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"The East Australian Current separates eastward as the Tasman Front at a variable latitude, reported between 28°S and 37°S. The cited study does not give stable whole-front endpoints or an along-flow length; do not add this branch to the East Australian Current's coastal floor. A 2019 review found the front rarely distinct in instantaneous fields; a single stable path length would overstate that evidence.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2017JC013097","source_decision":{"current_id":"tasman-front","name":"Tasman Front","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"The East Australian Current separates eastward as the Tasman Front at a variable latitude, reported between 28°S and 37°S. The cited study does not give stable whole-front endpoints or an along-flow length; do not add this branch to the East Australian Current's coastal floor. A 2019 review found the front rarely distinct in instantaneous fields; a single stable path length would overstate that evidence.","name_source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/2017JC013097","candidate_ids":["tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"eastward frontal current downstream of the East Australian Current","route_strategy_id":"dated_geometry","route_strategy_label":"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"The East Australian Current separates eastward as the Tasman Front at a variable latitude, reported between 28°S and 37°S. The cited study does not give stable whole-front endpoints or an along-flow length; do not add this branch to the East Australian Current's coastal floor. A 2019 review found the front rarely distinct in instantaneous fields; a single stable path length would overstate that evidence.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Use dated or explicitly averaged geometry, distinguish an open loop from a closed circuit, and compare repeated regimes before summarizing.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"tasman-front","label":"Historical composite and variable eastward pathways","audit_file":"research/tasman-front-composite-continuity-scope-audit.json","summary":"Historical composite paths combine different years and observation methods. A 2019 reassessment finds multiple pathways and questions a persistent narrow front across the central Tasman Sea. The 32–36 S meander band is not current width. A single dated axis, whole-current length and annual ranges remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796319300259","source_locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract and Introduction; author repository abstract. Historical comparison: Tilburg et al. (2001), Introduction, journal p. 2918, Figure 2 caption p. 2919.","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["east-australian"]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-source-scope-audit.v1","current_id":"tasman-front","as_of":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_source_scope_audit_not_canonical","source_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0924796319300259","source_citation":"Oke, Pilo, Ridgway, Kiss and Rykova (2019), A search for the Tasman Front, Journal of Marine Systems 199, 103217, doi:10.1016/j.jmarsys.2019.103217.","source_locator":"Publisher-indexed abstract and Introduction; author repository abstract. Historical comparison: Tilburg et al. (2001), Introduction, journal p. 2918, Figure 2 caption p. 2919.","source_access":"Oke et al. publisher-indexed abstract and Introduction and ANU repository abstract read. Direct publisher and author PDF retrieval failed; full 2019 article not inspected. Tilburg et al. author-hosted original PDF Introduction and Figure 2 caption read. No figure, velocity field or temperature section digitized.","scope":"Historical composite frontal pathway compared with a reassessment of central Tasman Sea continuity. Named inventory entry retained; no single instantaneous axis or whole-current endpoints admitted.","layer":"Historical infrared/front locations and climatological steric height relative to 2000 m are different diagnostic supports. Neither establishes a uniform-depth current axis or velocity-defined width.","time_convention":"Unsynchronized historical source sets and climatological interpretation remain separate from instantaneous and seasonal geometries.","observed_period":null,"historical_composite":{"source_url":"https://www.coaps.fsu.edu/bios/0110-2917.pdf","citation":"Tilburg, Hurlburt, O’Brien and Shriver (2001), The Dynamics of the East Australian Current System: The Tasman Front, the East Auckland Current, and the East Cape Current, JPO 31, 2917–2943.","locator":"Introduction, p. 2918; Figure 2 caption p. 2919.","source_sets":[{"original_source":"Mulhearn (1987), as described by Tilburg et al. (2001)","longitude_support_east":[153,164],"method":"Satellite infrared images","source_reported_period":"March 1982 to April 1985","source_reported_duration_months":29,"calendar_span_agrees_with_reported_duration":false,"duration_resolution":"Unresolved printed duration/date-span discrepancy; do not reinterpret 29 months as continuous coverage."},{"original_source":"Stanton (1979), as described by Tilburg et al. (2001)","longitude_support_east":[166,170],"method":"Five cruises","source_reported_period":"1966 to 1975"}],"described_departure_lon_lat":[153,-33],"described_meander_latitude_band_south":[32,36],"original_source_sets_directly_inspected":false,"figure_digitized":false,"composite_is_simultaneous_geometry":false,"longitude_coverage_gap_east":[164,166],"latitude_band_is_current_width":false,"composite_is_model_output":false},"continuity_assessment":{"source_convention":"Oke et al. (2019), indexed Introduction: CARS 2009 steric-height climatology, relative to 2000 m.","broad_weak_central_longitude_band_east":[158,168],"interpretation":"Time averaging can smear changing pathways; a persistent narrow coherent jet cannot be assumed from the mean. The reassessment also considers discontinuous streams and eddies.","continuous_front_absent_at_all_times":false,"mean_flow_implies_instantaneous_axis":false,"front_temperature_gradient_implies_current_width":false,"eddy_field_implies_no_eastward_transport":false,"coherent_route_constructed":false,"annual_geometry_playback_eligible":false},"name_equivalence_status":"Eastern extension of the EAC is a naming proposal in Oke et al. (2019); no automatic alias, new released identity or relation admitted.","whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"route_construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed_pending_geometry_definition","remaining_gates":["Define the target as a historical composite, a dated jet, a mean-flow connection or a transport corridor before measuring it.","Inspect original satellite/cruise sources and resolve the printed 29-month/date-span discrepancy; retain unsynchronized coverage and the 164–166 E gap.","Use compatible velocity fields to diagnose any current axis; classify interrupted or multiple branches rather than forcing one connecting polyline.","Keep East Australian coastal reach and New Zealand boundary currents separate; review any naming equivalence explicitly.","Recover matching dated transverse boundaries and repeated comparable seasonal samples before width or annual ranges."]},"source_sha256":"87d760963c9b6465312010ac60214d9808f9dfcceef485c30174595e354c5677"}]},{"id":"route-decision:tsushima","entity_id":"current:tsushima","label":"Tsushima Current","current_id":"tsushima","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"A segment of the Kuroshio system in NOAA's glossary.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"tsushima","name":"Tsushima Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"A segment of the Kuroshio system in NOAA's glossary.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":["tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"regional current","route_strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","route_strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"A segment of the Kuroshio system in NOAA's glossary.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:west-australian","entity_id":"current:west-australian","label":"West Australian Current","current_id":"west-australian","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","construction_status":"reference_path_not_constructed","candidate_count":0,"route_ids":[],"next_action":"Resolve the 1977 cyclonic-stream naming versus modern offshore northward flow using research/west-australian-current-naming-seasonal-scope-audit.json; its 800 km trough and 100-200 km width are unadmitted source context. Select layer/time-supported offshore velocity geometry and justify interface gates; coastal currents, particle release boundaries and inherited seasonal atlas patterns do not supply an axis.","scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"west-australian","name":"West Australian Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":[],"reference_path_decision":"reference_path_not_constructed","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"eastern boundary current","route_strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","route_strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","next_action":"Resolve the 1977 cyclonic-stream naming versus modern offshore northward flow using research/west-australian-current-naming-seasonal-scope-audit.json; its 800 km trough and 100-200 km width are unadmitted source context. Select layer/time-supported offshore velocity geometry and justify interface gates; coastal currents, particle release boundaries and inherited seasonal atlas patterns do not supply an axis.","strategy_next_action":"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[{"note":{"current_id":"west-australian","label":"Offshore West Australian versus coastal Leeuwin flow","audit_file":"research/west-australian-current-naming-seasonal-scope-audit.json","summary":"Modern West Australian Current means broad northward offshore flow, distinct from coastal southward Leeuwin. Andrews (1977) used the name for a cyclonic stream turning poleward: its reported 800 km trough extent and 100-200 km stream width remain historical source context, not admitted dimensions for this current or seasonal extrema. Whole-current axis, endpoints, width and annual ranges remain unresolved.","source_url":"https://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/west-australian-current/","source_locator":"West Australian Current definition paragraphs","observed_period":null,"related_current_ids":["leeuwin"],"supporting_sources":[{"label":"Historical naming and dimensions: Andrews (1977)","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0146629177905173","locator":"Publisher abstract","access":"Indexed abstract inspected; full paper unavailable and not reviewed."},{"label":"Separate coastal flows and model limits: Yit Sen Bull and van Sebille (2016)","url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2015JC011486","locator":"Introduction and sections 2.1-2.4","access":"Relevant full-text sections inspected; no model data or geometry extracted."}]},"document":{"schema":"osw.current-naming-scope-audit.v1","date":"2026-10-03","status":"editorial_scope_audit_not_scientific_approval","current_id":"west-australian","name":"West Australian Current","primary_definition":{"url":"https://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/west-australian-current/","access":"full_page_read_2026-10-03","locator":"Definition paragraphs","interpretation":"Broad offshore northward subtropical-gyre flow; distinct from coastal southward Leeuwin. Definition supplies no diagnosed axis, numeric endpoint coordinates or physical width."},"distinct_current_id":"leeuwin","coastal_study":{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921","citation":"Ridgway and Condie (2004), doi:10.1029/2003JC001921","access":"full_page_read_2026-10-03","locator":"Abstract; Introduction and Study Domain","interpretation":"Coastal shelf-edge system and its regional names; its 5500 km winter system length is not transferable to offshore West Australian Current."},"seasonal_context_lead":{"url":"https://library.dbca.wa.gov.au/static/FullTextFiles/065400.pdf","citation":"D’Adamo and Onton (2003), MMS-75/2003, dated 15 July 2003","access":"full_pdf_read_2026-10-03","locator":"Section 4 and Figure 12 caption, printed pp. 5 and 21 / PDF pp. 8 and 24","source_class":"government_synthesis_with_inherited_atlas_patterns","provenance_chain":["D’Adamo and Onton (2003)","Buchan and Stroud (1993)","US Navy (1976) Climatic Atlas of the World"],"interpretation":"Seasonal branching descriptions are inherited context, not newly acquired velocity geometry. Figure legend includes probable directions/speeds with insufficient data. Original atlas methodology and applicable samples require review.","original_atlas_read":false},"historical_naming_lead":{"url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0146629177905173","access":"publisher_indexed_abstract_read_2026-10-03; direct publisher full page unavailable; full paper not inspected","interpretation":"Abstract describes a cyclonic stream extending northeast from the Naturaliste Plateau and turning poleward at the coast. Its use of West Australian Current differs from the modern offshore northward definition; equivalence remains unreviewed.","citation":"Andrews (1977), Eddy structure and the West Australian current, Deep Sea Research 24(12), 1133-1148, doi:10.1016/0146-6291(77)90517-3.","locator":"Publisher abstract","reported_context":{"sampling":"Four cruises in the summers of 1972 and 1973; individual cruise dates unavailable in inspected abstract.","study_area_degrees":[8,8],"reported_trough_extent_km":800,"reported_stream_width_km":[100,200],"reported_scale_depth_m":370,"measurement_admission":"unadmitted_historical_source_context","modern_offshore_current_identity_equivalence_established":false,"width_limits_are_seasonal_extrema":false,"scale_depth_is_fixed_axis_layer":false,"trough_extent_is_modern_whole_current_length":false,"geometry_digitized":false}},"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"annual_length_range_km":null,"annual_width_range_km":null,"seasonal_route_playback_supported":false,"rejected_inferences":["No reuse of Leeuwin or 5500 km coastal-system path length.","No conversion of broad eastern Indian Ocean description into physical width or a representative single core.","No use of seasonal 20 S branching context as a universal whole-current endpoint.","No figure tracing or seasonal interpolation from inherited atlas patterns.","No transfer of the 1977 reported 800 km trough extent or 100-200 km cyclonic stream width into modern offshore-current dimensions before identity equivalence and full source methodology are reviewed.","The historical width interval is not a seasonal minimum/maximum range; a 370 m scale depth is not a uniform axis layer.","No substitution of coastal summer Capes/Ningaloo flow or deeper Leeuwin Undercurrent for the modern offshore West Australian Current.","Model particle release boundaries, sector limits and transport agreement are not current endpoint, width-edge or centerline diagnoses."],"remaining_gates":["Retrieve the full 1977 paper and resolve its poleward cyclonic-stream naming against the modern offshore northward flow; keep its reported dimensions in unadmitted source context meanwhile.","Choose representative layer and time support for a broad flow; consider a diagnostic flow corridor before a centerline.","Retrieve appropriate offshore velocity data and justify northern/southern interface gates independently of coastal-current geometry.","Read original seasonal atlas/data methodology before generating dated or seasonal routes.","Keep physical width, annual extrema and canonical measurement admission unresolved."],"modern_pathway_context":{"url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2015JC011486","citation":"Yit Sen Bull and van Sebille (2016), Sources, fate, and pathways of Leeuwin Current water in the Indian Ocean and Great Australian Bight: A Lagrangian study in an eddy-resolving ocean model, doi:10.1002/2015JC011486.","access":"Full publisher page retrieved; Introduction and sections 2.1-2.4 read on 2026-10-03; no figures digitized or model data acquired.","locator":"Introduction; 2.2 Eulerian TROPAC01 Validation at 32 S; 2.3 Lagrangian Particle Model; 2.4 coastal sectors.","interpretation":"Leeuwin, its deeper equatorward undercurrent, and inshore summer Capes/Ningaloo flows are separately named. Subtropical onshore supply and particle connectivity do not diagnose a whole West Australian Current axis.","validation_caution":"Section 2.2 reports lower modeled flow speeds compensated by broader flow in transport validation. Agreement of integrated transport does not independently validate width or a centerline.","model_support":"TROPAC01 1/10-degree model; 1960-2009 hindcast at five-day temporal means. This is model support, not West Australian Current observation dates.","model_release_sections_are_current_endpoints":false,"model_validation_transport_agreement_establishes_width":false,"leeuwin_dimensions_transfer_to_west_australian":false},"observed_period":null},"source_sha256":"55f4f9327a5211758bbaf422ff672a0fb39b63930c080df11677148d50cb5cdf"}]},{"id":"route-decision:west-greenland","entity_id":"current:west-greenland","label":"West Greenland Current","current_id":"west-greenland","strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["west-greenland-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","rank_eligible":false,"source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","source_decision":{"current_id":"west-greenland","name":"West Greenland Current","existing_length_evidence_status":"no_numeric_length","existing_scope":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","name_source_url":"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html","candidate_ids":["west-greenland-reference-path-candidate"],"reference_path_decision":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","published_length_rank_eligible":false,"ledger_kind":"regional current","route_strategy_id":"source_gated_regional_route","route_strategy_label":"Establish a sourced regional route","planning_status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval","planning_basis":"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","strategy_next_action":"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.","known_component_currents":[],"component_inventory_status":"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk"},"source_catalog_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_catalog_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","scope_reviews":[]},{"id":"route-decision:west-spitsbergen","entity_id":"current:west-spitsbergen","label":"West Spitsbergen Current","current_id":"west-spitsbergen","strategy_id":"resolve_naming_scope","strategy_label":"Resolve naming or extent convention","construction_status":"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending","candidate_count":1,"route_ids":["west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate"],"next_action":"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.","scope":"Marine Regions supplies one geographic point, not a centerline or endpoints; no comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.","status":"editorial_planning_crosswalk_